.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:524:
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:525:## 实测（5m 印刷页 1–11，PDF 10–20）
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:526:
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:527:11 页 → **4 个单元、55 道题（1–55 连续无缺号）、13 张编号插图 + 1 张无编号表格**。
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:528:15 张 SVG 全部通过保真自检，不匹配率 0.000%–0.093%（限 2%）。
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:529:跨页的第 29、36 题各由三段拼成，图自动跟到题上。
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:530:
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:531:## 已知行为
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:532:
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:533:- 一道题引用「图 6.2」时会保留对图 6 各子图的引用；每个实际 SVG 在练习区仍只展示一次
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:534:- `outside_ratio` 只是"文字占墨迹的比例"，不是错误指标
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:535:- 不做语义提取：表格一律当图裁，不拆成行列
.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md:536:- 一本书没抽完时，末尾会有若干块标着 `open` 接不上——这是正常的，只报告不失败
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:1:# Engineering
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:2:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:3:Human-authored architecture and development rules. This file defines how the product is built, how
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:4:code changes are made, and how they land. Section shape is fixed by `.intentfold/readme.md`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:5:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:6:The dependency inventory belongs to the lockfile; generated structure belongs to its generator.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:7:Record here only decisions, boundaries, and commands that the repository cannot explain by itself.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:8:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:9:> Consolidated on 2026-09-12 from the former architecture and development dimensions. Existing
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:10:> project decisions and boundaries were preserved. Pull-request landing commands were added later
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:11:> that day with explicit human authorization. The resource boundary was revised on 2026-09-13 by
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:12:> explicit human direction. Hosting and database-variable rules were revised on 2026-09-23
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:13:> with explicit human approval for the Render migration and Azure hosting cleanup.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:14:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:15:## Contract
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:16:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:17:**Stack**
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:18:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:19:- **tanstack-start** is the application framework — SSR full-stack, a single app in `app/`, React 19,
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:20:  TypeScript, Node 24. Vite builds it through the TanStack Start and Nitro plugins. This is the one
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:21:  supported application structure for this repo; a second app or a framework change is out of scope without
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:22:  a charter decision.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:23:- **`@tanstack/react-router`** is the router — file-based, under `app/src/routes/`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:24:- **Tailwind CSS 4** (+ tw-animate-css) is the styling authority; see `ui.md`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:25:- **zustand** is the client state library (`app/src/lib/layout-store.ts`).
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:26:- **PostgreSQL** via the `postgres` client is the datastore — the **shared Supabase project**, schema
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:27:  **`lemmadeck-schema`**, reached through `LEMMADECK_DATABASE_URL`. Never a second client.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:28:  `app/src/lib/db.ts` and the shared content helper require `LEMMADECK_DATABASE_URL`; missing
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:29:  configuration fails instead of falling back to another database. Render and local development
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:30:  use the same existing Supabase schema.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:31:- **Authentication is in-repo, no external provider**: scrypt password hashing (Node `crypto`) and an
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:32:  HMAC-signed httpOnly session cookie, both in `app/src/lib/session.server.ts`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:33:- **Content rendering**: markdown via `marked`; KaTeX is loaded from a CDN by the root document
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:34:  rather than bundled from npm.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:35:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:36:**Structure**
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:37:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:38:- **Repo layout**: `app/` = the web app, a **standalone project** with its
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:39:  own `package.json`/`package-lock.json`/`node_modules` — **there is no repo-root `package.json`**;
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:40:  commands run from `app/` or via `npm --prefix app`. `ssot-schemas/db-schemas/` = DB SSOT.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:41:  `ssot-resources/` is the only committed product-resource root: runtime public assets, design
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:42:  references, brand material, retained course sources, original textbooks, TOCs, durable
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:43:  transcriptions, final lessons, figures, answers and interactions all live below it. `.tmp/` is
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:44:  disposable scratch only and may be deleted as a whole after any ticket. Code-owned schemas,
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:45:  profiles, dependencies and test fixtures remain beside their code and are not product-resource
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:46:  roots. `.claude/skills/` = repository-local S10Y lesson and answer pipelines;
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:47:  `.agents/skills/` = project skills for modern figures, stories, the knowledge galaxy, and retained
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:48:  English generation tooling;
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:49:  `infra/` = deploy/substrate notes. No top-level `jobs/` — this project has no independently-packaged
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:50:  jobs. Root holds only cross-cutting files: the deploy `Dockerfile`, `.intentfold/`, `AGENTS.md`, and
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:51:  tooling config.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:52:- **Routes**: public learner routes are `index.tsx` and `_app/card.$id.tsx` for the textbook
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:53:  catalog and cards. The legacy English lesson and recitation paths redirect to the public landing
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:54:  page and render no English-learning UI. `login.tsx` remains the account entry.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:55:- **Domain libs** in `app/src/lib/`: `curriculum.ts` (course structure + lesson ordering/nav),
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:56:  `lessons.ts`, `stories.ts`, `quiz.ts` + `answer-normalize.ts` (practice, incl. `input`-mode
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:57:  server-side judging), `session*.ts` (auth), `db.ts` (postgres access, `search_path` = the project
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:58:  schema). `english.ts` remains only as preserved server/data capability and is not a learner-facing
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:59:  product module.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:60:- **DB access is server-only**: every read and write goes through `app/src/lib/db.ts`'s `sql()`. The
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:61:  browser never holds the connection string.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:62:- `app/vite.config.ts` sets `envDir: '..'` so build-time env resolves from the root `.env`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:63:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:64:**Key decisions**
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:65:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:66:- **Published content lives in the DB and is produced by named skills.** The sole math lesson entry is
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:67:  `.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson`: scanned textbook pages become faithful page artifacts, assembled
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:68:  lesson/exercise objects, and a `modern-us-neutral` edition under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:69:  `ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:70:  Modern figures are delegated to `ld-s10y-image`; answers and interaction specifications are added
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:71:  by `ld-s10y-answer`; their publishers upsert `sr_lessons`. The app reads the stored prose and
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:72:  exercise fragments at `/card/:id`. New math work does not use a concept ledger, neutral card tree,
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:73:  locale overlay, or retired concept-led lesson savers. Biographies use `sr-story`. Historical
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:74:  short-literature English rows and the `sr-voa1500` generator are retained but are not exposed by
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:75:  the application.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:76:- **Website hosting and content storage are independent.** Render runs the web application;
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:77:  the original shared Supabase project remains the content database. Hosting migration does not
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:78:  migrate the database. Identify the database by its authoritative connection, never by schema
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:79:  name alone. Azure model/image/TTS services remain generation dependencies, not website hosting.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:80:- **`ssot-schemas/db-schemas/lemmadeck.sql` is the single source of truth for the DB tables** — 18
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:81:  of them, generated from the live schema by STEMROBIN-124 and regenerated the same way whenever the
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:82:  schema changes deliberately. Reason: schema changes applied ad hoc drift away from anything
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:83:  reviewable, and a hand-maintained DDL drifts just as far (the file it replaced had fallen seven
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:84:  tables behind). It **describes**; it is never applied.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:85:- **Vitest uses a separate `app/vitest.config.ts`** because the TanStack Start Vite plugin is
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:86:  incompatible with the Vitest runner.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:87:- **Content tooling keeps its dependencies outside the deployed app.** Project skills under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:88:  `.agents/skills/` share that directory's package; `ld-s10y-lesson` owns its package and Python
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:89:  environment under `.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/`; `ld-s10y-answer` reuses the app's `postgres`
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:90:  dependency for its publishers.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:91:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:92:## Tools
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:93:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:94:**Pull-request landing**
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:95:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:96:Worktree tickets land through GitHub pull requests in `wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck`. Substitute the
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:97:ticket's recorded values for `<ticket-id>`, `<branch>`, and `<pr>`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:98:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:99:Find an existing PR:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:100:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:101:```bash
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:102:gh pr list --repo wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck --head <branch> --state all \
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:103:  --json number,title,url,state,headRefOid,baseRefName,mergeStateStatus,statusCheckRollup
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:104:```
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:105:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:106:Create one when absent:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:107:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:108:```bash
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:109:gh pr create --repo wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck --base main --head <branch> \
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:110:  --title "<ticket-id>" --body-file ".intentfold/tickets/<ticket-id>/handoff.md"
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:111:```
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:112:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:113:Read its current head, state, and checks:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:114:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:115:```bash
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:116:gh pr view <pr> --repo wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck \
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:117:  --json number,url,state,headRefOid,mergeStateStatus,statusCheckRollup
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:118:```
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:119:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:120:This repository currently configures no required GitHub checks, branch protection, rulesets,
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:121:overlap detector, or cap4 takeover gate. If that changes, update these Tools before landing the
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:122:next ticket. Merge with a merge commit, then confirm GitHub reports the merge commit:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:123:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:124:```bash
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:125:gh pr merge <pr> --repo wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck --merge
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:126:gh pr view <pr> --repo wang-chonghuan/lemmadeck --json state,mergedAt,mergeCommit
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:127:```
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:128:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:129:Do not pass `--delete-branch`; IntentFold cap4 deletes the local and remote ticket branches only
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:130:after the ticket backend reaches Done.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:131:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:132:**Mechanical defence**
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:133:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:134:Run once before handoff:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:135:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:136:```bash
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:137:python3 ssot-resources/audit.py
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:138:python3 ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/validate.py
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:139:node --test .agents/skills/lib/content-db.test.mjs
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:140:cd app && npm run test && npm run build
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:141:```
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:142:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:143:There is no separate lint or typecheck script today; `vite build` is the type-error boundary.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:144:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:145:**Architecture and generation**
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:146:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:147:- Build output: `app/.output` (`app/.output/server/index.mjs`).
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:148:- Content generation: never hand-write `sr_*` rows. Math starts at
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:149:  `.claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/SKILL.md`, delegates modern figures to `ld-s10y-image`, delegates
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:150:  answers and interaction specifications to `ld-s10y-answer`, and persists only through those
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:151:  skills' publishers. Its original scans, TOCs and durable artifacts live under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:152:  `ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/`; its renders, templates and previews live under `.tmp/`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:153:  Biographies use `sr-story`; retained short-literature English generation uses `sr-voa1500` but
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:154:  does not publish a learner-facing application surface.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:155:  Each skill's `SKILL.md` owns its exact generation and persistence commands.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:156:- DB schema: `ssot-schemas/db-schemas/lemmadeck.sql` describes the live schema. It is generated from
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:157:  the database, never hand-edited and never applied to it. The inspection command lives in
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:158:  `operations.md`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:159:- `.agents/skills/lib/content-db.mjs` owns DB URL resolution for content scripts under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:160:  `.agents/skills/`. Repository-local S10Y publishers live under `.claude/skills/`, read the
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:161:  repo-root `.env`, and must write through `LEMMADECK_DATABASE_URL`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:162:- `app/src/routeTree.gen.ts` is generated by the TanStack Start plugin and is never hand-edited.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:163:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:164:## Guidance
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:165:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:166:**No gratuitous dependencies.** If the existing architecture and stack can implement the requirement,
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:167:do not add, remove, or change any library. Solve it with what is here. A dependency change is
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:168:admissible only when the existing stack genuinely cannot meet the requirement and the ticket carries
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:169:that human decision.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:170:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:171:**Reuse before inventing.** Existing helpers, config paths, schemas, components, and SSOT files come
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:172:first. A second way to do something that already has a way is a defect, even when it works.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:173:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:174:**Respect ownership boundaries.** Find the domain lib that already owns the concept before adding a
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:175:new one — `curriculum.ts` owns structure and ordering, `quiz.ts` owns practice and judging,
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:176:`session*.ts` owns auth. A route file composes; it does not hold domain logic. Anything that touches
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:177:the DB goes through `db.ts`'s `sql()` even when a direct query would be shorter.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:178:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:179:**No dirty code.** No TEMP markers, degradation branches, or mocks standing in for a failed external
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:180:dependency. A failing external premise is a stop and a report.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:181:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:182:**Surgical changes.** Touch what the ticket needs and nothing else. Do not improve adjacent code,
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:183:reformat unrelated files, or fix things noticed in passing.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:184:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:185:**Uncertainty surfaces.** Prefer stopping and asking over inventing a fallback or hidden compatibility
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:186:layer.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:187:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:188:**DB access is server-only.** All reads and writes go through `app/src/lib/db.ts`'s `sql()`; the
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:189:browser never holds the connection string.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:190:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:191:**Content is DB-driven and skill-generated.** Never hand-write `sr_*` rows and never apply a schema
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:192:change ad hoc; both have exactly one path named in `## Tools`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:193:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:194:**Resource ownership is explicit.** Commit product resources only below `ssot-resources/`. Put
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:195:rebuildable renders, templates, previews, batch outputs and backups below `.tmp/`, and never make a
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:196:durable artifact depend on a `.tmp/` path. Keep schemas, profiles, dependency manifests and test
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:197:fixtures with the code that owns them.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:198:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:199:**Secrets.** `.env` holds DB and API secrets and is git-ignored. Never stage it, commit it, or echo
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:200:its contents; verify it is not staged before every commit.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:201:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:202:**Complexity hotspots**
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:203:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:204:TODO(human) — the former architecture dimension's `Complexity hotspots` section was an empty
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:205:placeholder awaiting real aborts. Lessons from things that went wrong belong here; it is what makes
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:206:the next grill sharper.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:207:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:208:## Redlines
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:209:
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:210:1. **Committing credentials, tokens, connection strings, or hidden account data** — forbidden
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:211:   outright, in source, mocks, ticket artifacts, and commits alike. Concretely: `.env` and `app/.env`
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:212:   never appear in `git status`'s staged set.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:213:2. **Discarding a change already present in a dirty worktree** — forbidden outright. It is the
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:214:   human's work until they say otherwise.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:215:3. **Sending an answer key to the client** — forbidden outright. The quiz question fetchers
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:216:   (`getLessonQuestions` / `getStoryQuestions` in `app/src/lib/quiz.ts`) must never include
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:217:   `correct_index`, `answer`, or `accept` in what they return; correctness is judged server-side in
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:218:   the `record*` server functions.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:219:4. **Opening a database connection anywhere under `app/` other than `app/src/lib/db.ts`** —
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:220:   forbidden outright. A second `postgres` client, or a connection string reaching any file under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:221:   `app/src/routes/` or any `.tsx`, is the crossing this names. Content scripts under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:222:   `.agents/skills/` are node CLIs governed by entry 9.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:223:5. **Adding, removing, or changing a dependency** — not without the human's explicit approval, and
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:224:   only when a ticket carries that decision.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:225:6. **Hand-editing a generated file** — forbidden outright: `app/src/routeTree.gen.ts`, anything under
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:226:   `app/.output/`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:227:7. **Changing the DB schema anywhere other than `ssot-schemas/db-schemas/lemmadeck.sql`** —
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:228:   forbidden outright. Ad hoc `ALTER`/`CREATE` against the shared server is drift.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:229:8. **Using a database connection other than `LEMMADECK_DATABASE_URL` for application or content
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:230:   access** — forbidden outright. `DATABASE_URL` and `EASYAPP_DATABASE_URL` are not aliases;
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:231:   same-named schemas on other servers are not the product database.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:232:9. **A content script under `.agents/skills/` calling `postgres(` directly** — forbidden outright.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:233:   Every content script connects through `.agents/skills/lib/content-db.mjs`.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:234:10. **Adding a repo-root `package.json`, or a second application** — not without the human's explicit
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:235:    approval. The standalone-`app/` layout is what the root `Dockerfile` builds.
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:236:11. **Committing a product resource outside `ssot-resources/`, or making durable content depend on
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:237:    `.tmp/`** — forbidden outright. Code-owned schemas, profiles, dependency files and test fixtures
.intentfold/charter/engineering.md:238:    remain beside code. `python3 ssot-resources/audit.py` is the mechanical boundary.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:1:---
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:2:name: intentfold
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:3:description: Load for ticket-based product development with the .intentfold harness, from initialization and filing through development, handoff and closure; also for multi-ticket delivery planning with cap5 or supervising one or more workers with cap6. Triggers include "intentfold", "cap1/cap2/cap3/cap3setup/cap3handoff/cap4/cap5/cap6", "开发这个工单", "准备开放开发", "开发完成，做 handoff", "建个工单", "拆单安排并行", "监督工人直到完成", and charter-directed deployment of merged code.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:4:---
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:5:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:6:# intentfold
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:7:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:8:One ticket at a time **per developer session**; a supervisor can coordinate several. `.intentfold/`
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:9:holds what persists, the ticket backend — **plane or linear**,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:10:whichever `project.json` names — holds the tickets. The ticket's acceptance criteria define acceptance;
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:11:the project's required mechanical checks still apply.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:12:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:13:The release version lives in `intentfold.json` (`version`). Usage declarations continue to record
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:14:the exact Git commit SHA, not this release number.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:15:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:16:**IntentFold** is the harness brand for three independent controls a project may name in
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:17:`charter/engineering.md`'s `## Tools`: an IntentFold process declaration, an overlap check before rebasing,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:18:and an optional cap4 takeover gate before merging. The declaration records the ticket, repository,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:19:and IntentFold version. The verifier checks the committed `handoff.md` directly from the PR head. It
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:20:is process evidence, not employee identity or proof that a binary ran.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:21:The overlap check detects when upstream and ticket changes touch the same code region. The ticket
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:22:developer resolves these overlaps and Git conflicts, verifies the result, and continues without an
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:23:additional team-leader approval. A cap4 takeover gate remains pending during
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:24:normal PR and review events, then releases the current head only after cap4 has armed auto-merge and
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:25:explicitly dispatched the trusted verifier.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:26:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:27:## Specification first
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:28:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:29:During planning and implementation, **do not use existing unit tests, for example unit tests
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:30:under `tests/`, as a reference for designing or changing code**. Do not infer requirements
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:31:from their assertions or preserve an obsolete implementation just to satisfy them. Design
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:32:from the approved ticket, Charter and valid external contracts; refactoring and optimization
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:33:remain available within that scope.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:34:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:35:Run the project's required unit tests **after implementation is ready for verification**.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:36:When one fails, judge both the test and the code against those same specifications:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:37:correct an outdated test or an assertion tied only to replaced implementation details;
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:38:correct the code when it violates a valid requirement. Do not weaken valid assertions,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:39:delete tests merely to get green, or infer expected values from the new code's output.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:40:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:41:Examples:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:42:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:43:- **Correct the test:** an approved refactor replaces per-item lookups with one batch
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:44:  lookup while preserving required results and error behavior. An old unit test in
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:45:  `tests/` asserts one private-helper call per item. Replace that obsolete assertion
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:46:  with the required behavior; do not restore the old call pattern.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:47:- **Correct the code:** the contract forbids reading another user's private record.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:48:  After a refactor, a unit test catches such a read succeeding. Fix the authorization
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:49:  regression; do not change the test to expect success.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:50:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:51:This does not prohibit reading production code, running the app, lint/type checks, or
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:52:consulting authoritative acceptance and API-contract specifications. Classify by purpose,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:53:not directory name: `tests/` may also contain those specifications. Required checks still
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:54:must pass; this rule changes what drives implementation, not the acceptance standard.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:55:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:56:## Proposed solutions
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:57:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:58:A developable ticket's `## Proposed solution` is advisory, not another requirement.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:59:Read it before choosing the implementation route and prefer its applicable parts rather
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:60:than starting over. Check its assumptions against the actual system; adapt or replace it
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:61:when incomplete, outdated, infeasible, or unnecessarily complex.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:62:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:63:Scope, explicit constraints, acceptance criteria and the Charter remain binding. Do not
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:64:silently demote an explicit user requirement into a suggestion. Explain material departures
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:65:briefly in the existing plan, draft or handoff; no separate report or extra approval round
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:66:is needed merely to change a proposal. A proposal neither replaces an agreed approach nor
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:67:skips the normal alignment step, and matching it is not an acceptance criterion.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:68:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:69:## Capability freshness gate
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:70:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:71:Before executing **any** IntentFold capability — cap1, cap2, cap3, cap3setup, cap3handoff, cap4, cap5, or cap6 —
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:72:run this once for the current capability invocation:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:73:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:74:```bash
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:75:skillhost update narrative-skills --agent <current-agent>
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:76:```
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:77:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:78:Use the current runtime's SkillHost agent name (`codex`, `claude`, `opencode`, `copilot`,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:79:`openclaw`, or `hermes`). If SkillHost is unavailable or the update fails, stop and report the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:80:failure; do not continue the capability with a stale skill. After a successful update, re-read the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:81:active SkillHost-linked `intentfold/SKILL.md` and the selected capability reference before
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:82:continuing. That re-read does not trigger a second update in the same invocation.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:83:Recurring cap6 inspections and resumes of that inspection loop are the same invocation,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:84:not reasons to update the skill at each inspection. A newly invoked child capability keeps its own gate.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:85:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:86:## Start here — what is being asked?
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:87:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:88:**Read this table before anything else and go where it points.** Not every request that mentions this
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:89:skill is one of its capabilities, and forcing one onto the nearest capability is the most common
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:90:way this skill gets misused.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:91:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:92:| The human wants… | Go to |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:93:|---|---|
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:94:| a `.intentfold/` harness in this repo | **cap1** — `references/capability-1-init/init.md` |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:95:| a ticket filed | **cap2** — `references/capability-2-ticket/create-ticket.md` |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:96:| IntentFold to develop a ticket autonomously, end to end — including a generic "开发这个工单" | **cap3** — `references/capability-3-develop/dev.md` |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:97:| the required IntentFold setup before vibe coding or another development skill | **cap3setup** — `references/capability-3-setup/setup.md` |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:98:| completed open-development work verified and handed off | **cap3handoff** — `references/capability-3-handoff/handoff.md` |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:99:| a verified ticket merged, landed, closed | **cap4** — `references/capability-4-close/close.md` |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:100:| a goal organized into the necessary tickets, parallel groups and dependencies | **cap5** — `references/capability-5-orchestrate/orchestrate.md` |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:101:| one existing ticket/worker, or an epic's workers, supervised through completion | **cap6** — `references/capability-6-supervise/supervise.md`; no mandatory cap5 or epic |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:102:| **to deploy** — "重新部署", "发布一下", "deploy this" | **Not a capability. Do not file a ticket.** See *Deploying on its own* below |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:103:| the app run, a page looked at, a log read | **Nothing here.** Follow `charter/operations.md` and do it |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:104:| a question answered about this project | **Nothing here.** Read `charter/`, answer, stop |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:105:| a code change, with no ticket for it | **cap2 first**, then cap3 or cap3setup. This is the case the no-ticket rule is for |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:106:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:107:When the request fits none of these, say so and ask — **do not map it onto the closest capability.**
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:108:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:109:## Supervised delivery
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:110:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:111:For cap5/cap6 and their explicitly supervised children, read
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:112:`references/common/supervision.md`. It is the scoped override for finish, Grill, recoverable
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:113:stops, the delivery decision and next-ticket selection below. Defaults are **no recurring
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:114:monitoring, delegated ordinary decisions, and `finish: review`**: develop and verify, then
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:115:keep the preview ports running for human review. Requested monitoring runs every **10 minutes**;
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:116:automatic merge/closure or deployment requires its own explicit authorization.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:117:Unsupervised cap1-cap4 behavior is unchanged.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:118:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:119:cap5's arrangement must pass `references/gate-5-orchestrate/gate.md` inline before filing
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:120:or dispatch. cap6 reuses the existing handoff decision, not a new review pipeline.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:121:Session names, model resolution, bootstrap and opt-in recurring continuation live only in
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:122:`references/common/supervision-sessions.md`.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:123:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:124:## Deploying on its own
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:125:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:126:Deploying already-merged code is **not a product change and needs no ticket**. `charter/operations.md`
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:127:says it in its own words: a ticket ends at merge, and deploying is a separate, deliberate act. Three
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:128:steps, and this skill contributes nothing else:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:129:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:130:1. Read `charter/operations.md`, including its `## Redlines`. A first-time or destructive deploy needs the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:131:   human; a routine redeploy of an already-deployed service does not.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:132:2. Do exactly what `operations.md` says. No assumed platform, no invented command. If it does not say how,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:133:   that is a stop.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:134:3. **Confirm it actually took** by its post-deploy check — hit the URL, look at the response. *"The
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:135:   deploy command exited 0"* is not confirmation.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:136:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:137:The same three steps run inside cap4 for an `auto-deploy` ticket. Standalone, they are the whole job.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:138:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:139:## Why this skill is shaped the way it is
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:140:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:141:The point of this skill is **speed with a trace**, not assurance. Autonomous cap3 has exactly one
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:142:thinking step (a grill, before the code); cap3setup instead establishes the required boundary and
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:143:leaves the development method open. Both routes have one IntentFold proof step in cap3handoff: run
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:144:the product, check the AC, and look at the result once through the human's request. Everything
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:145:else is just a record so a human can see later what happened. **No repeated review passes, no
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:146:regression suite added by the workflow, no timeline, no ADR log.** Multi-ticket coordination belongs to cap5/cap6, not a developer's ticket. If you find
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:147:yourself about to verify something a second time, stop — that is the thing this skill exists to not
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:148:do.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:149:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:150:What this skill refuses is checking that is **frequent, repeated, and scattered everywhere** — the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:151:same question asked at five points because nobody could say which point was the real one. It does not
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:152:refuse checking. **At a major joint, check.** The joints are few and named: before development starts
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:153:(cap3's grill and route lookup, or cap3setup's boundary briefing), at the cap3handoff proof step, and
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:154:before an irreversible act in cap4. A check at a joint costs seconds and catches what cannot be
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:155:undone afterwards; the same check sprinkled through every step is the bureaucracy this skill exists
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:156:to avoid. Judge a proposed check by **where** it sits, not by whether it is a check.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:157:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:158:## Persistent layer
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:159:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:160:```text
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:161:.intentfold/
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:162:  readme.md            # session entry: what to read, in what order
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:163:  project.json         # project/main/deploy/tickets + each service's main port and ticket prefix
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:164:  charter/             # human-owned intent — read it; write it only when the human asks
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:165:    product.md         #   product purpose, users, value, non-goals
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:166:    engineering.md     #   architecture, development rules, checks, and landing
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:167:    ui.md              #   design system and interface constraints
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:168:    operations.md      #   local runtime, acceptance evidence, deploy, and operations
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:169:  tickets/<ticket-id>/ # ticket.json (mode/stage/finish/branch/base/ports)  draft.md  plan.md  ac.md
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:170:                       # grill.md  handoff.md  intentfold-usage.json  rework.md  tmp/
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:171:  tmp/                 # project scratch
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:172:```
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:173:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:174:`tmp/` directories and env files are git-ignored; everything else is committed.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:175:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:176:In commands, `<intentfold-skill>` means the loaded skill directory containing this `SKILL.md`.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:177:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:178:The four-file Charter contract is exact. A project that still has `charter/readme.md`, `dev.md`,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:179:`arch.md`, `runbook.md`, `qa.md`, or `devops.md` has not migrated; cap3 and cap3setup stop rather
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:180:than interpreting both layouts or combining human-owned files automatically.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:181:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:182:## The charter's shape — four sections, and how each is used
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:183:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:184:Every charter file is made of these four, always in this order and always all four. They are not
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:185:strength levels — they are four different things to state, and **each is consumed at a different
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:186:moment, in a different way**. `.intentfold/readme.md` carries the full rules and the tests for
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:187:deciding where a line goes; this is what the flow needs to know:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:188:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:189:| Section | States | The flow's use of it |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:190:|---|---|---|
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:191:| **Contract** | what the artifact is | **referenced while authoring** — built from, never audited against at the end |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:192:| **Tools** | commands, paths, ports, URLs, viewports | **looked up at the moment of acting**, run as written; never recalled from earlier in the run, never restated into a plan or a ticket |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:193:| **Guidance** | how to do the work | **followed while writing**, judged by the author. **Nothing in this skill reviews a diff against Guidance** — that is deliberate, and adding such a review is the bureaucracy this skill refuses |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:194:| **Redlines** | the boundary | **looked up before the action**, table-style, never judged |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:195:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:196:**All four headings appear in every charter file**, in this order; a section with nothing to say
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:197:keeps its heading and stays empty. An empty section states that the dimension has nothing of that
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:198:kind — a missing heading would instead read as "somebody forgot", and it would break the addressing
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:199:the capabilities rely on. Redlines live in the file whose dimension they belong to; there is **never
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:200:a separate redline file**.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:201:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:202:**A rule is worth more mechanised than emphasised.** Where a Contract fact or a Redline can be
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:203:checked by a command, the charter names that command in `Tools` and the build fails — that beats the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:204:same rule written more forcefully, and it is why the flow needs no review pass.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:205:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:206:**Where the flow touches each section**, once each, and nowhere else:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:207:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:208:- **cap3 step 1 or cap3setup step 1** reads `Contract` + `Guidance` as the constraints the ticket is
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:209:  built under.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:210:- **cap3 step 4** looks the planned route up against `Redlines` — before any code exists, because an
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:211:  approval collected afterwards is not an approval.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:212:- **cap3setup step 5** briefs the relevant `Redlines` before its open development phase, since
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:213:  IntentFold does not own a route to look up.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:214:- **cap3handoff** reads `Tools` at the moment of acting (start the product, run the checks) and runs
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:215:  the project's mechanical defence once before the handoff.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:216:- **cap4** runs the mechanical defence once on the final branch only when rework or synchronization
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:217:  requires it, as its close reference specifies. It reads `engineering.md`'s PR commands at the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:218:  moment it uses them, and a deploying ticket reads `operations.md`'s `Tools` and `Redlines` at the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:219:  moment of deploying.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:220:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:221:Nothing reads the charter to audit finished work. That is the duplication this arrangement removes.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:222:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:223:**Requirements stay authoritative in the ticket backend** — read the ticket live each time through
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:224:**n-plane** or **n-linear** as `project.json` `tickets.system` says. There is no `req.md`. `ac.md` is
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:225:only the executable check plan and must match the live acceptance criteria. The routing, delegation
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:226:rule and per-backend content language are in `references/common/ticket-backend.md`; read it before the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:227:first ticket read or write of a run.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:228:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:229:## Ticket types
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:230:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:231:Set by the human when the ticket is filed — or, for a ticket the human wrote by hand in the backend's
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:232:UI, inferred once from its prose when cap3 or cap3setup structures it
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:233:(`references/capability-2-ticket/create-ticket.md`, "A ticket someone wrote by hand"). **The agent
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:234:never changes a type** — in particular never promotes an `express` ticket into the full flow because
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:235:the work turned out bigger. If a type looks wrong, say so and stop; the human re-decides.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:236:Cap5 may select the parent/child types under its explicit orchestration delegation, as cap2 describes.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:237:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:238:| Type | What it is | Worktree | Autonomous `plan.md` / `ac.md` | Autonomous grill | Proof | `handoff.md` |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:239:|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:240:| **story / enabler / fix** | shipped-code work | yes | yes | yes | playwright AC check | yes |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:241:| **chore** | **changes no code** — generating data, changing a configuration, a runtime or dashboard operation | yes | no | no | whatever settles its criterion — usually a command, the running product when only it can show it | yes |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:242:| **express** | the human wants to change something **directly on main**, interactively; unavailable when the project requires PRs or IntentFold | **no** | no | no | playwright AC check | yes |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:243:| **seed** | an idea or note, never developed | no | no | no | none | no |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:244:| **epic** | a multi-ticket delivery outcome and coordination, not code | no | no | no | overall outcome using child evidence | no; backend closing record |
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:245:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:246:cap3setup writes `ac.md` but no IntentFold `plan.md` or grill; the open development middle chooses
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:247:its own planning and interaction method.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:248:An epic stays in the backend: cap5 arranges it, cap6 supervises it, cap4 closes its overall
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:249:outcome without Git artifacts. It is not a developed type and never enters cap3's worktree flow.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:250:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:251:**Autonomous cap3 has one alignment with the human before any code, in one of two orders.** When the human opens the run
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:252:with *"discuss the approach first"*, cap3 talks it through and records the agreed approach in
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:253:`draft.md`, then plans from it — and does not grill. Otherwise it drafts `plan.md` / `ac.md` first and
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:254:grills them. Exactly one of the two runs; a draft is what the human reaches for when the ticket is
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:255:unclear, is wrong, or when they already know how they want it built.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:256:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:257:Every developed type ends in a `handoff.md` — that is what makes the work readable later, and it is
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:258:the one artifact none of them skip. A **seed** gets no `tickets/<id>/` directory at all and lives only
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:259:in the ticket backend.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:260:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:261:`chore` gets a worktree like any other work even though it writes no code: its output still gets
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:262:committed, and an isolated checkout is what keeps a half-done configuration change out of main.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:263:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:264:## The capabilities
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:265:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:266:Paths are in the routing table above; this is what each one is for.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:267:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:268:1. **cap1 Initialize** — "初始化 intentfold". Lands `.intentfold/` in this repo and pushes it.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:269:2. **cap2 File a ticket** — "建个工单". The only birth channel for a product change.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:270:3. **cap3 Autonomous development** — the complete built-in path: the same required opening boundary
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:271:   as cap3setup, IntentFold's own plan / grill / implementation, then the cap3handoff proof boundary.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:272:3setup. **cap3setup Open development setup** — creates the worktree, `ticket.json`, `ac.md`, and
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:273:   boundary briefing, then stops. The middle may be ordinary vibe coding with the current agent or
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:274:   any other development skill. IntentFold does not own that middle.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:275:3handoff. **cap3handoff Verify and hand off** — accepts the committed result of autonomous or open
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:276:   development, runs the AC and mechanical defence, writes `handoff.md` and the usage declaration,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:277:   then finishes per the effective `finish` recorded in `ticket.json`. It does not merge or close the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:278:   ticket; that remains cap4.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:279:4. **cap4 Close a ticket** — "合了这个工单", "关掉这个工单". Rework record → rebase → merge → stop the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:280:   service → sync `.env` → deploy if requested → close → clean up → update the main checkout. **Every irreversible action lives
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:281:   here.** cap3 calls it directly in an auto mode; in the default 验证模式 the human's approval usually
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:282:   arrives in a later session, and this is what that session runs.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:283:5. **cap5 Orchestrate delivery** — understand/reuse, minimal decomposition, epic and child tickets,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:284:   parallel groups and actual dependency conditions. Planning alone does not start workers.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:285:6. **cap6 Supervise execution** — bind current work; default to development and a running preview
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:286:   for human review, without recurring monitoring. When requested, inspect every 10 minutes,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:287:   correct drift and advance only to the authorized finish, including closure/deployment if approved.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:288:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:289:## Finish mode — declared on the ticket when it is filed
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:290:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:291:Carried as the ticket's `Finish` row. **Default is 验证模式, including cap6** — a ticket that says
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:292:nothing waits for the human after verification. Monitoring alone does not change its finish;
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:293:supervised delegation uses `references/common/supervision.md`.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:294:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:295:- **`review` — 验证模式 (default)** — develop, check the AC, then **leave the service running** and
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:296:  send cap3handoff's review message: the URL, what to check and where, and what was decided for
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:297:  the human. Do not merge, do not close. Wait.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:298:- **`auto-merge` — 自动合并** — the human said so when filing. Develop, check the AC, merge, sync
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:299:  `.env` back, clean up, close, pick the next ticket and keep going without asking.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:300:- **`auto-deploy` — 自动部署** — auto-merge, **then deploy** per `charter/operations.md` and confirm the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:301:  deploy actually took, then close and continue.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:302:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:303:A human instruction when cap3 or cap3setup starts overrides the row for that development run. Resolve
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:304:the effective value once, record it as `ticket.json` `finish`, and leave a ticket comment when it
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:305:differs from the row. The description itself is never amended.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:306:Supervised next-ticket selection is limited to assigned, dependency-ready work.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:307:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:308:## Hard rules
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:309:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:310:- **No change to the product without a ticket.** File one first (cap2) if the user asks for a code
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:311:  change and there is none. **Scope: the repo's shipped content.** Operating what is already landed is
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:312:  not a product change and needs no ticket — deploying merged code, running the app, reading a log,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:313:  answering a question about the project, looking something up in the charter. When in doubt: does it
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:314:  add a commit to the product? Then it needs a ticket.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:315:- **One backend, and it decides the language.** `project.json` `tickets.system` picks plane or linear,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:316:  and every ticket read and write goes through that skill — never a hand-written API call. All ticket
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:317:  text, comments included: **linear → English, required; plane → Chinese by default**, English only
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:318:  when the human explicitly asks. See `references/common/ticket-backend.md`.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:319:- **Autonomous cap3 grills once, before the code, on story / enabler / fix only** —
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:320:  `references/common/grill.md`. Persist the complete question batch, recommendations and reasons
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:321:  in the ticket's `grill.md` before asking or self-adjudicating; record answers in that same file.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:322:  cap3setup has no IntentFold grill because its development middle is
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:323:  open. `chore` and `express` have no grill. The grill's coverage is the same in every mode;
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:324:  default autonomous cap3 asks the human only the questions that pass the grill's bar, one line
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:325:  each, and continues without stopping when none do;
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:326:  the agent self-adjudicates **only** when the ticket's `Grill: self` row says the human authorized
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:327:  it, and stops when it hits a question only a human can answer. The explicit supervised delegation in
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:328:  `references/common/supervision.md` also grants self-adjudication within its scope.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:329:- **Irreversible or externally-consequential actions need the human.** Creating or deleting cloud
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:330:  resources, publishing publicly, sending mail or messages to real recipients, deleting or polluting
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:331:  production data, spending money. Route around it, or stop and hand it over — never approximate and
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:332:  never decide on the human's behalf. This holds on every project; it is not something a charter
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:333:  grants away.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:334:- **Redlines are lookup, and they live in the charter file they belong to** — as that file's closing
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:335:  `## Redlines` section, which **every charter file carries, empty when there is nothing to forbid**
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:336:  (the shape is `.intentfold/readme.md`'s; it is stated there and nowhere else). `charter/ui.md` owns
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:337:  the token-registry one, `charter/operations.md` the deploy ones, and so on. **There is never a separate
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:338:  `redline.md`**: a cross-cutting file is organised by severity while the rest are
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:339:  organised by subject, so it attracts every important rule and fills with copies of them. The
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:340:  prohibitions that hold on every project — destructive external writes, irreversible production data,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:341:  spend — are hard rules here instead. Check them before acting; do not ask "is this a big deal?", check
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:342:  whether the action is listed. Each entry says whether it is forbidden outright or needs the human's
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:343:  approval.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:344:- **The charter is binding, not advisory.** `charter/product.md`, `charter/engineering.md`,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:345:  `charter/ui.md`, and `charter/operations.md` are **obeyed**. They are not style suggestions,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:346:  defaults to weigh against convenience, or something a deadline overrides. When the ticket cannot
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:347:  be done without breaking one of them, that is a **stop**: say which rule, say why the ticket needs
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:348:  it broken, and hand it to the human. Deciding it yourself is never available, and "the charter
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:349:  didn't literally cover this case" is not permission — ask.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:350:- **The charter binds the agent, not the human.** It exists to stop the agent changing things on
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:351:  its own, not to stop the human changing them. When the human explicitly asks for something the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:352:  charter rules out, that request is the authorization to change the charter: amend the rule in
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:353:  the same ticket so it matches what was asked, and say in the ticket which rule changed and why.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:354:  Do not stop to ask for the charter change a second time, and do not file it as "confirm before
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:355:  changing the charter". The stop above is for conflicts the agent's own route or inference
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:356:  creates, never for what the human asked for. The every-project hard rules (destructive external
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:357:  writes, irreversible production data, spend) still need their own explicit approval.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:358:- **Charter is human-owned; report drift, do not quietly fix it.** The agent may edit `charter/` when
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:359:  the human asks for that edit, and only for what they asked. A human request that only works if a
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:360:  charter rule changes is such an ask, for that rule. What stays forbidden is editing it on
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:361:  the agent's own initiative — deciding mid-ticket that a rule is inconvenient and rewriting it, or
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:362:  "correcting" the charter to match code the agent just wrote. Prove the drift, say what is stale,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:363:  and let the human decide what the charter should say. The document that constrains every ticket
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:364:  must not be the document every ticket rewrites to suit itself. The human's preferences are read
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:365:  from earlier tickets' grill answers and rework asks (`references/common/grill.md`) and are not
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:366:  written into the charter or any other file.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:367:- **IntentFold usage and overlap resolution stay separate.** Usage records the ticket identity,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:368:  repository, and IntentFold version once after handoff. It does not identify the PR author, duplicate
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:369:  Git's content hashing, bind a Git tree, or include an overlap report. The overlap check compares
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:370:  upstream and ticket code regions; the ticket developer owns resolution and verification, regardless
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:371:  of PR author. IntentFold does not require an additional team-leader approval for this work.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:372:- **Cap4 takeover is not a signature and does not duplicate usage evidence.** When a project
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:373:  configures it, normal PR and review events leave the required integrity status pending. Cap4 reads
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:374:  the current head, arms auto-merge first, then dispatches the trusted verifier for that exact head.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:375:  A new head invalidates the authorization. The takeover proves only that cap4 controls the merge;
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:376:  its resumable post-merge steps still establish backend closure and cleanup.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:377:- **Legacy IntentFold machinery is a stop.** If `charter/engineering.md` still names a comment-based approval
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:378:  override, CI private-key signing, a CI-signed full-tree manifest, or a close-marker PR, report the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:379:  exact stale entries and wait for a human-authored charter migration. An overlap detector, cap4
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:380:  takeover dispatch, and combined `intentfold / integrity` check are current controls, not legacy ones.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:381:  If an existing project still enforces team-leader overlap approval, report that policy mismatch for
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:382:  an explicitly authorised migration; do not bypass its required check or fabricate an approval.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:383:- **Acceptance follows the AC**, checked against the running product, alongside the project's
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:384:  existing required checks. Do not add unrelated regression or coverage work. Apply
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:385:  **Specification first** above when unit tests fail. "The code implements it" is never evidence.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:386:- **Cap4 closure conditions are a closed set.** AC must pass, and only the existing explicit
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:387:  conditions in `references/capability-4-close/close.md` apply. Never add a closure condition,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:388:  promote an optional check into a requirement, or infer a gate from a tool's default behavior.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:389:  Cap4's reference owns the waiting and commit rules; it is not a new verification round.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:390:- **No fake progress.** No TEMP markers, no degradation branches, no mock standing in for a failed
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:391:  external dependency. A dead credential or unreachable service is a stop, not a workaround.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:392:- **Ticket-owned `.env` key changes sync back to the main checkout on every merge**, with the old file
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:393:  backed up first. Preserve unrelated main-checkout values. Never commit env files. See
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:394:  `references/common/worktree-env-port.md`.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:395:- **A dev server never outlives the run that started it.** Stopped at close, and stopped when a run
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:396:  stops for any other reason. The only exception is 验证模式, where it is deliberately left running
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:397:  for the human, or the short supervised delivery checkpoint described in the shared contract;
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:398:  then cap4 kills it. Kill by the port `handoff.md` records as actually used,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:399:  not the computed one, and confirm the port is free.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:400:- **cap4 first checks whether the PR is already merged, then rebases the ticket branch onto freshly
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:401:  fetched `origin/<main>` and lands it through the project's pull-request workflow.** Push the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:402:  rebased ticket branch explicitly to its remote branch with `--force-with-lease`. When the project
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:403:  configures cap4 takeover, arm auto-merge for the exact current head before dispatching
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:404:  authorization for that head; otherwise use the project's named required-check and merge commands.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:405:  Never move local `main` as part of another ticket.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:406:  The only exception is an express ticket in a project whose charter explicitly has no PR or
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:407:  IntentFold requirement; cap4 handles that local-main route separately.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:408:- **The ticket developer owns overlap and conflict resolution.** When configured, cap4 runs the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:409:  overlap detector before rebasing onto current remote main. Overlap is an inspection signal, not an
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:410:  approval gate. Resolve using both branches' intent, preserve unrelated upstream changes, verify
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:411:  affected criteria, and continue cap4 without an additional team-leader approval. See cap4 step 3.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:412:- **Unresolvable intent is a stop, not every Git conflict.** Do not blindly select ours or theirs.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:413:  If the intended combined behaviour cannot be established, abort the rebase, retain the branch and
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:414:  worktree, and ask the human with the conflict evidence.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:415:- **IntentFold usage is recorded once after the handoff is complete.** The repository verifier checks
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:416:  the ticket, repository, IntentFold version, and committed `handoff.md`. It does not require
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:417:  employee registration, an SSH key, or equality between the declaration creator and the PR author.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:418:- **Never `rm -rf`.** Worktree deletion is `git worktree remove`'s job; generated artifacts worth
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:419:  keeping are **moved** out, not removed. Recursive deletes are unnecessary here and are commonly
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:420:  blocked by local safety policy anyway.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:421:- **`handoff.md` freezes at the first-delivery commit.** Commit each human- or authorized
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:422:  supervisor-requested rework round once, using that ask as the commit message. Do not combine
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:423:  separate requested rounds into one commit. Cap4's own incidental changes and required records
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:424:  are different: avoid new commits where possible, otherwise batch them into one final commit,
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:425:  not one per workflow step. Reconstruct `rework.md` **once** at close from the diff since first
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:426:  delivery. No per-round bookkeeping artifact. Never edit a frozen handoff to keep it current.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:427:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:428:## Stop conditions
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:429:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:430:For supervised work, first apply `references/common/supervision.md`: a repo-correctable
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:431:failure or ordinary design question stays within the delegation. A coordination checkpoint
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:432:goes to the next inspection only when monitoring is active; otherwise report unresolved
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:433:blockers in the worker's session, not to an absent supervisor. Only the affected step waits;
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:434:other authorized work continues. Necessary checks still must pass. The preservation rules
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:435:below also apply to such checkpoints.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:436:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:437:**When to stop:** an external premise failed; a redline blocks the only route; self-adjudication hit a
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:438:question only a human can rule; the AC still fails after three attempts; an unresolved conflict; a
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:439:required-check failure.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:440:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:441:**What stopping looks like — the same every time**, so a later session finds a known state:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:442:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:443:- Leave a ticket comment with the cause and the evidence.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:444:- **Ticket stays In Progress.** It is not done and it is not abandoned.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:445:- **Worktree and branch stay.** They are what a resumed run picks up; deleting them is what makes the
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:446:  work unrecoverable.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:447:- **Dev server stops**, port confirmed free.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:448:- Say plainly in the worker session what is left where; an active cap6 monitor reads that
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:449:  checkpoint. Without monitoring, report directly to the human.
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:450:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:451:## Partner skills
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:452:
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:453:**n-plane** *or* **n-linear** — whichever backend `project.json` names, for every ticket read and write —
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:454:and **n-grill** (the grill's coverage) are used by the flow itself. Deployment has no assumed
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:455:tooling — follow whatever `charter/operations.md` says; **n-easyapp** is used only when that file
/Users/yong/.agents/skills/intentfold/SKILL.md:456:or the human names it.
